---
import ProjectModal from "../components/ProjectModal.astro";
---

<ProjectModal
  id="merchant-recommendation-project"
  ariaLabel="Merchant Recommendation System project"
>
  <article class="merchant-project">

    <section class="project-hero">
      <div class="project-hero-top">
        <span>04 / SELECTED WORK</span>
        <span>CLIENT-FACING PROJECT</span>
      </div>

      <h1>Merchant<br />Recommendation System</h1>

      <p class="project-tagline">
        The right product,<br />
        for the right customer.
      </p>

      <p class="project-supporting">
        A client-facing recommendation and demand intelligence system built
        for a plumbing merchant. The project uses historical customer and
        sales behaviour to personalise product discovery, suggest useful
        basket additions and help the business understand future product demand.
      </p>

      <div class="project-meta">
        <span>CLIENT-FACING</span>
        <span>RECOMMENDATION SYSTEMS</span>
        <span>GRU</span>
        <span>TENSORFLOW</span>
        <span>PROPHET</span>
        <span>STREAMLIT</span>
        <span>PANDAS</span>
        <span>PYTHON</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="intro-grid">
      <div class="intro-block">
        <span class="section-number">01</span>

        <h2>What the client needed.</h2>

        <p>
          The merchant has a large catalogue of plumbing, heating,
          ventilation, fittings, tools and related products. The challenge was
          helping customers find products that are actually relevant to them,
          while also identifying complementary items that naturally belong
          together.
        </p>

        <p>
          The client also wanted to make better use of historical sales data
          behind the scenes, particularly for understanding product demand
          and supporting stock planning.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="intro-block">
        <span class="section-number">02</span>

        <h2>What I worked on.</h2>

        <p>
          I designed a recommendation framework that changes behaviour
          depending on what the system knows about the customer.
        </p>

        <p>
          New visitors receive sensible popularity-based recommendations,
          returning customers receive personalised predictions from their
          purchase history, and basket activity triggers related-product
          recommendations based on historical buying behaviour.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also developed a product-level demand forecasting pipeline and
          built the recommendation scenarios into an interactive Streamlit
          application for the client.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>UNDER THE HOOD</span>

        <h2>
          One dataset.<br />
          Several ways to help.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-flow">
        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Sales history</strong>
          <small>
            Customer, product, quantity, price, discount and transaction history
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Preparation</strong>
          <small>
            Invalid records removed and customer purchase histories prepared
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Customer context</strong>
          <small>
            New visitor, returning customer, basket activity or combined context
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Recommendation</strong>
          <small>
            Popularity, GRU sequence modelling and item co-occurrence
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Demand intelligence</strong>
          <small>
            Monthly product-level forecasting using sales and behavioural features
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span>06</span>
          <strong>Client demo</strong>
          <small>
            Interactive Streamlit interface for testing realistic customer scenarios
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-detail">
        <div>
          <span>DESIGN PRINCIPLE</span>

          <h3>
            Context decides<br />
            the model.
          </h3>

          <p>
            I did not try to force every customer through the same model.
            A completely new visitor does not have enough information for
            meaningful personalisation, while a returning customer or an
            active basket provides much stronger behavioural signals.
          </p>

          <p>
            The system chooses a recommendation strategy according to what
            information is actually available.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle-card">
          <span>EXAMPLE FLOW</span>

          <strong>
            No history?<br />
            Start with what works.
          </strong>

          <small>
            New customer → popular products<br />
            Purchase history → GRU recommendations<br />
            Basket activity → frequently bought together
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="scenario-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>RECOMMENDATION STRATEGY</span>

        <h2>
          Different customer.<br />
          Different signal.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="scenario-grid">
        <article class="scenario-card">
          <span>01 / NEW VISITOR</span>

          <h3>Start with popularity.</h3>

          <p>
            With no customer history or basket information, recommendations
            fall back to products that consistently appear in historical
            purchases.
          </p>

          <div class="scenario-model">
            GLOBAL POPULARITY
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="scenario-card featured">
          <span>02 / RETURNING CUSTOMER</span>

          <h3>Learn what comes next.</h3>

          <p>
            Customer purchases are converted into ordered product sequences.
            A GRU model learns repetition, transitions and purchasing patterns
            to predict likely future products.
          </p>

          <div class="scenario-model">
            GRU SEQUENTIAL MODEL
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="scenario-card">
          <span>03 / ACTIVE BASKET</span>

          <h3>Look at what belongs together.</h3>

          <p>
            Historical orders are analysed to find products that commonly
            appear together, allowing the system to suggest useful additions
            while the customer is actively shopping.
          </p>

          <div class="scenario-model">
            ITEM CO-OCCURRENCE
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="features-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>MORE THAN ONE MODEL</span>

        <h2>
          What the system actually does.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Cold-start recommendations</h3>
          <p>
            Uses historical product popularity when there is no customer
            history available, ensuring new visitors still receive useful
            recommendations.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Sequential personalisation</h3>
          <p>
            A GRU-based recommender learns ordered customer purchase behaviour,
            repeat buying patterns and product transitions to generate
            personalised Top-N predictions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Frequently bought together</h3>
          <p>
            Item co-occurrence analysis identifies products that historically
            belong together, supporting basket expansion and practical
            cross-selling.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Commercial recommendations</h3>
          <p>
            Recommendation logic can also consider discounted products and
            business-priority items rather than relying entirely on machine
            learning output.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Demand forecasting</h3>
          <p>
            Historical sales are converted into monthly product-level time
            series and forecast using Prophet with price, discount, time and
            regional holiday features.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>Parallel forecasting</h3>
          <p>
            A custom Python pipeline processes and forecasts many products
            concurrently using ThreadPoolExecutor, with tqdm providing live
            progress throughout longer model runs.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="forecast-section">
      <span class="forecast-number">03</span>

      <div>
        <span class="forecast-label">FROM RECOMMENDATIONS TO STOCK PLANNING</span>

        <h2>
          What might sell next,<br />
          and how much?
        </h2>

        <p>
          The same sales history used to understand customer behaviour is
          also transformed into monthly product-level time series for demand
          forecasting.
        </p>

        <p>
          The pipeline incorporates quantities, pricing, discounts,
          seasonality and regional holiday effects before fitting product-level
          Prophet models.
        </p>

        <div class="forecast-metrics">
          <div>
            <span>MAPE</span>
            <small>Percentage error</small>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>SMAPE</span>
            <small>Symmetric percentage error</small>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>WAPE</span>
            <small>Volume-weighted error</small>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="testing-note">
          Forecasting experiments were designed to compare product-level model
          behaviour rather than claim a single universal accuracy figure across
          the entire catalogue.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="iteration-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>ITERATION</span>

        <h2>
          It grew past<br />
          one recommender.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="iteration-grid">
        <div class="iteration-column">
          <span>RECOMMENDATION</span>
          <p>
            The first idea developed into a scenario-based recommendation
            architecture with separate strategies for anonymous visitors,
            returning customers and active baskets.
          </p>
          <p>
            I later added discounted-product recommendations, business-priority
            ranking and a Streamlit interface so the client could interact with
            the different behaviours directly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="iteration-column">
          <span>FORECASTING</span>
          <p>
            The demand pipeline evolved from basic product forecasting into a
            configurable monthly processing system with external regressors,
            holiday features, lag experiments and per-product validation.
          </p>
          <p>
            Performance became its own engineering problem, leading to
            experiments with Dask, process-based parallelism, thread-based
            execution, regressor pruning and live progress monitoring.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-ending">
      <p class="ending-label">
        Client-facing recommendation system developed for a plumbing merchant.
      </p>

      <h2>
        Help customers choose.<br />
        Help the merchant prepare.
      </h2>

      <p class="ending-supporting">
        Recommendation systems, customer behaviour modelling and demand
        forecasting built around the same real-world sales problem.
      </p>
    </section>

  </article>
</ProjectModal>

<style>
  .merchant-project {
    width: 100%;
    color: #25301f;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 8% 8%, #E8E2CD 0%, transparent 34%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 93% 17%, #81916E 0%, transparent 32%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 74% 73%, #A1AC8D 0%, transparent 37%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 15% 90%, #657856 0%, transparent 31%),
      linear-gradient(135deg, #C7CBB4 0%, #D1D3BD 48%, #C7CBB4 100%);
  }

  .merchant-project strong { color: inherit; }

  .project-hero {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 88vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 70px;
  }

  .project-hero-top {
    position: absolute;
    top: 28px;
    left: 70px;
    right: 90px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    color: #3F5238;
  }

  .project-hero h1 {
    max-width: 1250px;
    margin: 0;
    font: 400 clamp(4rem, 10vw, 9.5rem)/.86 "Instrument Serif", serif;
    letter-spacing: -.055em;
  }

  .project-tagline {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 42px 0 20px;
    font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3.4vw, 3.6rem)/.98 "Instrument Serif", serif;
  }

  .project-supporting,
  .intro-block p,
  .architecture-detail p,
  .scenario-card p,
  .feature-card p,
  .forecast-section p,
  .iteration-column p,
  .ending-supporting {
    max-width: 720px;
    font: 1rem/1.6 "Courier Prime", monospace;
    color: #3F5238;
  }

  .project-supporting { margin: 0; }

  .project-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .project-meta span {
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border: 1px solid #25301f33;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    letter-spacing: .025em;
  }

  .demo-section { padding: 0 70px 110px; }

  .demo-video-frame {
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: #3F5238;
  }

  .demo-video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .section-heading > span,
  .architecture-detail span,
  .forecast-label,
  .ending-label,
  .iteration-column > span {
    font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
  }

  .section-heading { margin-bottom: 54px; }

  .section-heading h2 {
    max-width: 950px;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6vw, 7rem);
    line-height: .9;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .intro-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 70px;
    padding: 20px 70px 130px;
  }

  .intro-block {
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid #25301f33;
  }

  .section-number {
    font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    color: #657856;
  }

  .intro-block h2 {
    margin: 20px 0;
    font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 4vw, 4.6rem);
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .intro-block p { margin: 0 0 18px; }

  .architecture-section {
    padding: 110px 70px;
    color: #E8E2CD;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 20%, #657856 0%, transparent 35%),
      linear-gradient(135deg, #31422C, #3F5238 52%, #657856);
  }

  .architecture-section .section-heading > span,
  .architecture-detail span { color: #C7CBB4; }

  .architecture-flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr) auto) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .architecture-node {
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 205px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: 23px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    border: 1px solid #ffffff35;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .architecture-node span,
  .architecture-node small { font-family: "Courier Prime", monospace; }

  .architecture-node span {
    font-size: .7rem;
    color: #A1AC8D;
  }

  .architecture-node strong {
    font: 400 1.82rem/1 "Instrument Serif", serif;
    color: #E8E2CD;
  }

  .architecture-node small {
    max-width: 170px;
    font-size: .78rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: #C7CBB4;
  }

  .architecture-arrow { color: #A1AC8D; }

  .architecture-detail {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: 60px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 100px;
    padding-top: 80px;
    border-top: 1px solid #ffffff30;
  }

  .architecture-detail h3 {
    margin: 16px 0 24px;
    font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: .93;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .architecture-detail p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #E8E2CD;
  }

  .principle-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 32px;
    border: 1px solid #ffffff35;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #ffffff0d;
  }

  .principle-card strong {
    font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem)/.98 "Instrument Serif", serif;
  }

  .principle-card small {
    color: #C7CBB4;
    font: .78rem/1.7 "Courier Prime", monospace;
  }

  .scenario-section {
    padding: 130px 70px;
    background: #E8E2CDCC;
  }

  .scenario-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .scenario-card {
    min-height: 390px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #25301f25;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #C7CBB4BB;
  }

  .scenario-card.featured {
    color: #E8E2CD;
    background: #3F5238;
  }

  .scenario-card > span {
    font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    color: #657856;
  }

  .scenario-card.featured > span { color: #A1AC8D; }

  .scenario-card h3 {
    margin: auto 0 20px;
    font: 400 clamp(2.3rem, 3.6vw, 4rem)/.92 "Instrument Serif", serif;
  }

  .scenario-card p { margin: 0 0 26px; }

  .scenario-card.featured p { color: #E8E2CD; }

  .scenario-model {
    width: fit-content;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font: .68rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    letter-spacing: .05em;
  }

  .features-section {
    padding: 130px 70px;
    background: #C7CBB4DD;
  }

  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .feature-card {
    min-height: 300px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 27px;
    border: 1px solid #25301f20;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #E8E2CDBB;
  }

  .feature-card:nth-child(even) { background: #A1AC8DAA; }

  .feature-card > span {
    font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    color: #657856;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    margin: auto 0 20px;
    font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.7rem)/.95 "Instrument Serif", serif;
  }

  .feature-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: .95rem;
  }

  .forecast-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    padding: 130px 70px;
    background: #81916E;
  }

  .forecast-number {
    font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    color: #3F5238;
  }

  .forecast-section h2 {
    max-width: 1050px;
    margin: 18px 0 28px;
    font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 7.5rem);
    line-height: .88;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .forecast-section p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #2F4029;
  }

  .forecast-metrics {
    max-width: 760px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .forecast-metrics div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 7px;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #25301f25;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .forecast-metrics span {
    font: 1.5rem "Instrument Serif", serif;
  }

  .forecast-metrics small {
    font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace;
    color: #3F5238;
  }

  .testing-note {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-top: 28px !important;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid #25301f25;
    font-size: .82rem !important;
  }

  .iteration-section {
    padding: 130px 70px;
    background: #E8E2CDE8;
  }

  .iteration-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 70px;
  }

  .iteration-column {
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid #25301f25;
  }

  .iteration-column > span { color: #657856; }

  .iteration-column p { margin: 24px 0 0; }

  .project-ending {
    min-height: 80vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 120px 70px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 90% 20%, #A1AC8D 0%, transparent 32%),
      linear-gradient(135deg, #C7CBB4, #E8E2CD);
  }

  .project-ending h2 {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
    font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8rem);
    line-height: .84;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .ending-supporting { margin: 0 0 44px; }

  @media (min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1350px) {
    .architecture-flow {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 18px;
    }

    .architecture-arrow { display: none; }
    .architecture-node { min-height: 170px; }
    .architecture-node small { max-width: none; }
    .scenario-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .scenario-card { min-height: 300px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .project-hero {
      min-height: 88dvh;
      padding: 90px 20px 40px;
    }

    .project-hero-top {
      top: 20px;
      left: 20px;
      right: 72px;
      gap: 12px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      font-size: .6rem;
    }

    .project-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 14vw, 5.5rem);
    }

    .project-tagline {
      margin: 30px 0 18px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 10vw, 2.8rem);
    }

    .project-supporting,
    .intro-block p,
    .scenario-card p,
    .feature-card p,
    .forecast-section p,
    .iteration-column p {
      font-size: .9rem;
    }

    .project-meta {
      gap: 7px;
      margin-top: 22px;
    }

    .project-meta span {
      padding: 8px 10px;
      font-size: .62rem;
    }

    .demo-section { padding: 0 16px 80px; }
    .demo-video-frame { border-radius: 16px; }

    .intro-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 60px;
      padding: 20px 20px 90px;
    }

    .architecture-section,
    .scenario-section,
    .features-section,
    .forecast-section,
    .iteration-section,
    .project-ending {
      padding: 90px 20px;
    }

    .section-heading h2 {
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 14vw, 5rem);
    }

    .architecture-flow {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .architecture-arrow {
      text-align: center;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }

    .architecture-node { min-height: 145px; }
    .architecture-node small { max-width: none; }

    .architecture-detail {
